From da25e6e53926d39bfc9189f0a911bc597008ebd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VLCKit Aloha Release <devnull@alohabrowser.com>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 12:36:54 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] apple/build.sh: compile libvlc with -fvisibility=hidden
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add -fvisibility=hidden to the CFLAGS/CXXFLAGS/OBJCFLAGS exported by
set_host_envvars before libvlc's ./configure. This makes every C function
inside libvlc's per-plugin static libraries (libavformat_plugin.a,
libavcodec_plugin.a, …) compile with hidden Mach-O visibility.

Why: the Aloha iOS app links its own FFmpeg.framework next to VLCKit's
static archive. Without hidden visibility, VLC's avformat wrapper symbols
(`_avformat_OpenDemux`, `_avformat_CloseDemux`, …) plus FFmpeg's
re-exported internals all surface as public `T` in nm output, where they
collide with the consumer's FFmpeg. The 2026-05-15 spec's done-definition
explicitly requires:

    nm -arch arm64 VLCKit | grep -E ' T _(av|avcodec|avformat|avutil|swscale|swresample|avfilter|postproc|avdevice)_' | wc -l
    # expected: 0

VLCKit's own ObjC public API (VLCMediaPlayer et al.) is untouched —
Objective-C class metadata is registered via the runtime, not via the
ELF/Mach-O export table.
---
 extras/package/apple/build.sh | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/extras/package/apple/build.sh b/extras/package/apple/build.sh
index 8157d10c5d..388c291096 100755
--- a/extras/package/apple/build.sh
+++ b/extras/package/apple/build.sh
@@ -747,7 +747,13 @@ echo ""
 echo "Building VLC for $VLC_HOST_ARCH"
 
 # Set flags for VLC build
-set_host_envvars "-g"
+#
+# Aloha: -fvisibility=hidden hides every C function compiled into libvlc's
+# static archive (including VLC's own avformat/avcodec module wrappers like
+# `_avformat_OpenDemux`). When VLCKit ships as a static .framework, the
+# consuming app can link a separate FFmpeg.framework without symbol
+# collisions — required by the 2026-05-15 spec's nm acceptance criterion.
+set_host_envvars "-g -fvisibility=hidden"
 
 # Combine settings from config file
 VLC_CONFIG_OPTIONS=( "${VLC_CONFIG_OPTIONS_BASE[@]}" )
-- 
2.44.0

